# WE 32100 Microprocessor SLEIGH specification
#
# References:
#   - WE 32100 Microprocessor Information Manual, AT&T (Jan 1985)
#   - SIMH 3B2 emulator (open-simh/simh, 3b2_cpu.c/h) by Seth Morabito
#   - MAME WE32100 disassembler (we32100d.cpp) by AJR
#
# Architecture notes:
#   - 32-bit big-endian CISC processor
#   - Data memory accesses are big-endian and word-aligned
#   - Instruction operand descriptors encode multi-byte immediates and
#     displacements in LITTLE-ENDIAN byte order within the instruction stream
#   - Variable-length instructions (1 to ~20 bytes)
#   - Stack grows UPWARD (push: store at SP, then SP += size)
#   - 16 registers: R0-R8 general, R9=FP, R10=AP, R11=PSW, R12=SP,
#     R13=PCBP, R14=ISP, R15=PC

define endian=big;
@include "WE32100.sinc"
